    "term":'<p class="qz-txt"><b>A 13-year-old male presents to the ED for worsening facial swelling over the past 5 days. He has been having progressive shortness of breath over the past 6 weeks and a new dry cough. On exam, he has facial plethora, increased work of breathing with minimal exertion, and a notably distended right jugular vein.</b></p><div class="key1"><p><b>What is the etiology of his symptoms?</b></p></div>',
